title: mf repo restore
tags: [[CLI command]] Storage
kind: reference
summary: Put a backup of a repository back (the most recent one by default)

Puts back `--from` or the most recent backup, after checking it; the current store is
set aside, never deleted. A repository that no longer loads is named by `--path` (or
`--metafolder`). Everything written since the backup is lost: run `mf reconcile`
afterwards ([[Backups and restore]]).
